WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — deterministic-null (180s) Narrator Hari

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:07.189
First, most AI benchmarks skip a zero-model control group that tests what simple lookup already solves.

2
00:00:07.749 --> 00:00:10.769
Second, on bounded math and database tasks,

3
00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:14.982
a frozen lookup table matched cloud AI on nine of ten tests.

4
00:00:15.542 --> 00:00:18.603
Third, on open coding tasks AI leaped ahead,

5
00:00:18.603 --> 00:00:23.542
while caching verified answers cut repeat energy three point six times.

6
00:00:24.102 --> 00:00:31.098
Modern AI evaluations routinely compare one language model against another, leaving a foundational scientific question

7
00:00:31.098 --> 00:00:36.730
unmeasured: how much task completion actually needed a neural network at decision time, and how

8
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:42.422
much could a fixed integer lookup procedure over verified prior examples already solve for free?

9
00:00:42.982 --> 00:00:49.160
Just as clinical drug trials seal their treatment protocols before patients enroll, we anchored our frozen

10
00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:56.445
lookup store's digital fingerprint onto Bitcoin calendar proofs before public randomness beacons existed, and capped per-task

11
00:00:56.445 --> 00:01:02.215
helper code at four kilobytes and fifty thousand operations so no hidden solver could sneak inside.

12
00:01:02.775 --> 00:01:09.530
At test time, the control loop observes an input, reduces features using pure sixty-four-bit signed integers

13
00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:16.973
with zero floating-point instructions, probes a read-only memory-mapped hash table in half a microsecond, and acts with

14
00:01:16.973 --> 00:01:23.478
zero model calls. Rust, Go, Python, Julia, and C plus plus match bit-for-bit across one million records.

15
00:01:24.038 --> 00:01:31.689
Subtracting control accuracy from neural accuracy reveals a sharp boundary governed by how often genuinely unseen patterns

16
00:01:31.689 --> 00:01:39.152
arrive in the workload stream. Where structural templates saturate early, frozen integer lookup matches giant models at

17
00:01:39.152 --> 00:01:46.866
zero call cost; where open-world software recombines freely, neural synthesis shines and then seeds future instant lookups.

18
00:01:47.426 --> 00:01:54.350
This three-dimensional crystal depicts our frozen binary lookup table locked before public randomness rounds existed.

19
00:01:54.350 --> 00:02:01.570
Paired evaluation lanes route every fresh test problem simultaneously to zero-model controls, classical deductive solvers,

20
00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:08.495
local open-weight models on Apple Silicon, and six multi-vendor cloud frontier systems under identical scoring rules.

21
00:02:09.055 --> 00:02:15.935
Single-turn cloud models beat the frozen table on just one of ten bounded cells, while multi-turn clause feedback

22
00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:22.633
solved fifty of fifty logic formulas that a free classical solver also closed. Across public coding suites and

23
00:02:22.633 --> 00:02:30.792
six real upstream repository bugs—five patched and replayed at zero model calls—frontier models leaped up to ninety-five points ahead.

24
00:02:31.352 --> 00:02:38.071
Every measurement boundary stays completely transparent from start to finish. Local workstation energy comes from built-in

25
00:02:38.071 --> 00:02:43.745
Apple chip counters rather than an external wall meter, closed cloud server watts are recorded strictly

26
00:02:43.745 --> 00:02:50.409
as unavailable instead of guessed from fleet averages, and busy-host baseline drift drops net subtractions automatically.
